        "id": 15060,
        "name": "Kratos13",
        "username": "Kratos13",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/65b543/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-04-16T03:11:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So I'm assuming Handelabra did their homework so this is more just confirmation:</p><p>The Title Chaos Lord states when a Player plays more than 3 cards in one turn, place this title under that player's Hero Character Card...</p><p>I guess there is some fine print here that states that the Villain counts as a Player, Title cards are played by the Villain and the title goes to either the Villain Character target card or the Villain card with the highest HP?</p><p>I had Chaos Lord go to Impassable Andolin (Kaargra was not flipped) on Kaargra's turn who played two cards plus a Title card after a target was destroyed.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:47:19.234Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
